---@class sentry.GetOrganizationReplayRequest
---@field organization_id_or_slug string The ID or slug of the organization the resource belongs to.
---@field replay_id string The ID of the replay you'd like to retrieve. It is a 32-character hexadecimal string.
---@field statsPeriod? string This defines the range of the time series, relative to now. The range is given in a `<number><unit>` format. For example `1d` for a one day range. Possible units are `m` for minutes, `h` for hours, `d` for days and `w` for weeks. You must either provide a `statsPeriod`, or a `start` and `end`.
---@field start? string This defines the start of the time series range as an explicit datetime, either in UTC ISO8601 or epoch seconds. Use along with `end` instead of `statsPeriod`.
---@field ["end"]? string This defines the inclusive end of the time series range as an explicit datetime, either in UTC ISO8601 or epoch seconds. Use along with `start` instead of `statsPeriod`.
---@field field? sentry.GetOrganizationReplayRequestFieldList Specifies a field that should be marshaled in the output. Invalid fields will be rejected.
---@field project? sentry.GetOrganizationReplayRequestProjectList A list of project IDs or slugs to filter by.
---@field projectSlug? sentry.GetOrganizationReplayRequestProjectSlugList A list of project slugs to filter your results by.
---@field environment? sentry.GetOrganizationReplayRequestEnvironmentList The environments to filter by.
---@field sort? string The field to sort the output by.
---@field sortBy? string The field to sort the output by.
---@field orderBy? string The field to sort the output by.
---@field query? string A structured query string to filter the output by.
---@field queryReferrer? string Internal referrer identifier used for query tracing.
---@field per_page? number Limit the number of rows to return in the result.
---@field cursor? string The cursor parameter is used to paginate results. See [here](https://docs.sentry.io/api/pagination/) for how to use this query parameter

