---@field ["end"]? string The end of the period of time for the query, expected in ISO-8601 format. For example, `2001-12-14T12:34:56.7890`.
---@field timestamp? string The timestamp of an event in the trace, as an ISO 8601 string or Unix timestamp in seconds. When passed, the query is narrowed to a window around this time, which is faster than searching the full time range.
---@field include_uptime? sentry.GetOrganizationTraceMetaRequestIncludeUptime|string Set to `1` to include uptime check counts in the response. Defaults to `0` (disabled).

---@alias sentry.GetOrganizationTraceMetaRequestIncludeUptime "0"|"1"

