---@field event_id string The ID of the event. It is a 32-character hexadecimal string as reported by the client.
---@field environment? sentry.GetProjectEventRequestEnvironmentList The name of environments to filter by.
---@field start? string The start of the period of time for the query, expected in ISO-8601 format. For example, `2001-12-14T12:34:56.7890`.
---@field ["end"]? string The end of the period of time for the query, expected in ISO-8601 format. For example, `2001-12-14T12:34:56.7890`.
---@field statsPeriod? string The period of time for the query, will override the start & end parameters, a number followed by one of: - `d` for days - `h` for hours - `m` for minutes - `s` for seconds - `w` for weeks For example, `24h`, to mean query data starting from 24 hours ago to now.
---@field statsPeriodStart? string How long ago the query period starts, in the same format as `statsPeriod`. Must be sent with `statsPeriodEnd`, and is ignored when `statsPeriod` is sent.
---@field statsPeriodEnd? string How long ago the query period ends, in the same format as `statsPeriod`. Must be sent with `statsPeriodStart`, and is ignored when `statsPeriod` is sent.
---@field collapse? sentry.GetProjectEventRequestCollapseList Parts of the response to skip computing. Specify `adjacentEvents` to skip looking up the neighboring events in the issue; `nextEventID` and `previousEventID` are then always `null`. Unknown values are ignored.

