---@class sentry.GetTraceItemStatisticsRequest
---@field organization_id_or_slug string The ID or slug of the organization the resource belongs to.
---@field statsType sentry.GetTraceItemStatisticsRequestStatsTypeList The statistics to compute over the matching trace items.
---@field project? sentry.GetTraceItemStatisticsRequestProjectList The IDs or slugs of projects to filter by. Project slugs are unique within each organization. Omit this parameter to include all accessible projects. `-1` is also accepted to include all accessible projects. For example, the following are valid parameters: - `/?project=1234&project=56789` - `/?project=android&project=javascript-react` - `/?project=-1`
---@field environment? sentry.GetTraceItemStatisticsRequestEnvironmentList The name of environments to filter by.
---@field statsPeriod? string The period of time for the query, will override the start & end parameters, a number followed by one of: - `d` for days - `h` for hours - `m` for minutes - `s` for seconds - `w` for weeks For example, `24h`, to mean query data starting from 24 hours ago to now.
---@field start? string The start of the period of time for the query, expected in ISO-8601 format. For example, `2001-12-14T12:34:56.7890`.
---@field ["end"]? string The end of the period of time for the query, expected in ISO-8601 format. For example, `2001-12-14T12:34:56.7890`.
---@field query? string Sentry [search syntax](https://docs.sentry.io/concepts/search/) to filter trace items before computing statistics.
---@field substringMatch? string Restrict results to attribute names containing this substring (case-sensitive).
---@field traceItemsLimit? number Maximum number of trace items to sample when computing statistics. Defaults to `1000`, which is also the maximum.
---@field itemType? sentry.GetTraceItemStatisticsRequestItemType|string The trace item dataset to compute statistics for. Defaults to `spans`. * `spans` * `occurrences`
---@field cursor? string A pointer to the last object fetched and its sort order; used to retrieve the next or previous results.

---@alias sentry.GetTraceItemStatisticsRequestEnvironmentList string[]

---@alias sentry.GetTraceItemStatisticsRequestItemType "spans"|"occurrences"

