---@class sentry.ListOrganizationIssuesRequest
---@field organization_id_or_slug string The ID or slug of the organization the resource belongs to.
---@field environment? sentry.ListOrganizationIssuesRequestEnvironmentList The name of environments to filter by.
---@field project? sentry.ListOrganizationIssuesRequestProjectList The IDs or slugs of projects to filter by. Project slugs are unique within each organization. Omit this parameter to include all accessible projects. `-1` is also accepted to include all accessible projects. For example, the following are valid parameters: - `/?project=1234&project=56789` - `/?project=android&project=javascript-react` - `/?project=-1`
---@field statsPeriod? string The period of time for the query, will override the start & end parameters, a number followed by one of: - `d` for days - `h` for hours - `m` for minutes - `s` for seconds - `w` for weeks For example, `24h`, to mean query data starting from 24 hours ago to now.
---@field statsPeriodStart? string How long ago the query period starts, in the same format as `statsPeriod`. Must be sent with `statsPeriodEnd`, and is ignored when `statsPeriod` is sent.
---@field statsPeriodEnd? string How long ago the query period ends, in the same format as `statsPeriod`. Must be sent with `statsPeriodStart`, and is ignored when `statsPeriod` is sent.
---@field start? string The start of the period of time for the query, expected in ISO-8601 format. For example, `2001-12-14T12:34:56.7890`.
---@field ["end"]? string The end of the period of time for the query, expected in ISO-8601 format. For example, `2001-12-14T12:34:56.7890`.
---@field groupStatsPeriod? sentry.ListOrganizationIssuesRequestGroupStatsPeriod|string The timeline on which stats for the groups should be presented.
---@field shortIdLookup? sentry.ListOrganizationIssuesRequestShortIdLookup|string If this is set to `1` then the query will be parsed for issue short IDs. These may ignore other filters (e.g. projects), which is why it is an opt-in.
---@field query? string An optional search query for filtering issues. A default query will apply if no query is set. For all results use this parameter with an empty string.
---@field sort? sentry.ListOrganizationIssuesRequestSort|string The sort order of the view. Options include 'Last Seen' (`date`), 'First Seen' (`new`), 'Trends' (`trends`), 'Events' (`freq`), 'Users' (`user`), 'Date Added' (`inbox`), and 'Recommended' (`recommended`).
---@field limit? number The maximum number of issues to return. The maximum is 100.
---@field expand? sentry.ListOrganizationIssuesRequestExpandList Additional data to include in the response.
---@field collapse? sentry.ListOrganizationIssuesRequestCollapseList Fields to remove from the response to improve query performance.
---@field cursor? string A pointer to the last object fetched and its sort order; used to retrieve the next or previous results.

