---@class sentry.UpdateACustomInboundFilterRequest
---@field organization_id_or_slug string The ID or slug of the organization the resource belongs to.
---@field project_id_or_slug string The ID or slug of the project the resource belongs to. Project slugs are unique within each organization.
---@field filter_id string The ID of the custom inbound filter.
---@field dataType sentry.UpdateACustomInboundFilterRequestDataType|string The data the filter matches against. `all` is the catch-all: it filters every data type Sentry ingests, including ones added later, and accepts only the conditions that every data type carries a field for. * `all` * `error` * `log` * `metric` * `span`
---@field conditions sentry.UpdateACustomInboundFilterRequestConditionsList Conditions are combined with AND: an event must match every condition to be filtered out. There is no OR between conditions, so e.g. two release conditions can express a range (`gte 2.0` and `lt 4.0`). To broaden matching, widen a condition's values or add separate filters.
---@field name? string|distilled.Null A human-readable label for the filter.
---@field active? boolean Whether the filter drops matching data. An inactive filter is kept but ignored.

---@class sentry.UpdateACustomInboundFilterRequestConditionsItem
---@field type sentry.UpdateACustomInboundFilterRequestConditionsItemType|string The field the condition matches against. Every `dataType` accepts `release` and `ip_address`. In addition, `error` accepts `error_type`, `error_message` and `geo_country_code`, `log` accepts `log_message`, and `metric` accepts `metric_name`. `span` and `all` accept no other types. * `error_type` * `error_message` * `log_message` * `metric_name` * `release` * `ip_address` * `geo_country_code`
---@field operator? sentry.UpdateACustomInboundFilterRequestConditionsItemOperator|string How the field compares to `value`. `glob` matches the field against each value as a glob pattern. `equals`, `starts_with`, `contains` and `ends_with` match the field against each value case-insensitively, with every character read literally; `does_not_start_with`, `does_not_contain` and `does_not_end_with` match when no value does. `cidr` matches `ip_address` against each value as an address or a CIDR range, and `not_cidr` matches when no value does. `gt`, `gte`, `lt` and `lte` compare one value as a version and only apply to `release`. * `glob` * `equals` * `starts_with` * `contains` * `ends_with` * `does_not_start_with` * `does_not_contain` * `does_not_end_with` * `cidr` * `not_cidr` * `gt` * `gte` * `lt` * `lte`
---@field value sentry.UpdateACustomInboundFilterRequestConditionsItemValueList The values the field is compared to. The condition matches when any value matches, so multiple values act as OR; a negated operator matches when none does. A version comparison takes one release with a version such as `1.2.0` or `myapp@1.2.0`. A comparison with a package only applies to releases of that package.

---How the field compares to `value`. `glob` matches the field against each value as a glob pattern. `equals`, `starts_with`, `contains` and `ends_with` match the field against each value case-insensitively, with every character read literally; `does_not_start_with`, `does_not_contain` and `does_not_end_with` match when no value does. `cidr` matches `ip_address` against each value as an address or a CIDR range, and `not_cidr` matches when no value does. `gt`, `gte`, `lt` and `lte` compare one value as a version and only apply to `release`.
---
