---Status of the monitor. Disabled monitors will not accept events and will not count towards the monitor quota.
---
---* `active`
---* `disabled`
---@alias sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorRequestStatus "active"|"disabled"

---@class sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponse
---@field id string ID of the monitor
---@field name string Name of the monitor
---@field slug string Slug that identifies the monitor in the organization
---@field status sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseStatus Status of the monitor. Disabled monitors don't accept check-ins
---@field isMuted boolean Whether incidents are muted in all of the monitor's environments
---@field isUpserting boolean Whether the most recent check-in was an upsert check-in
---@field config sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseConfig Configuration of the monitor
---@field dateCreated string When the monitor was created (ISO 8601)
---@field project sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseProject Project the monitor belongs to
---@field environments sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseEnvironmentsList Environments the monitor has received check-ins for
---@field owner sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseOwner|distilled.Null Team or user that owns the monitor. Null when there's no owner

---Configuration of the monitor
---@class sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseConfig
---@field schedule_type sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseConfigScheduleType Type of schedule: crontab or interval
---@field schedule sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseConfigSchedule Schedule of the monitor: a crontab string, or a [value, unit] pair for intervals, such as [1, "day"]
---@field checkin_margin number|distilled.Null How long in minutes after the expected check-in time to wait before the check-in counts as missed
---@field max_runtime number|distilled.Null How long in minutes a check-in can stay in progress before it counts as failed
---@field timezone string|distilled.Null Timezone the schedule is evaluated in, as a tz database name
---@field failure_issue_threshold number|distilled.Null Number of consecutive missed or failed check-ins before an issue is created
---@field recovery_threshold number|distilled.Null Number of consecutive successful check-ins before the issue is resolved
---@field alert_rule_id number|distilled.Null ID of the alert rule linked to the monitor

---Schedule of the monitor: a crontab string, or a [value, unit] pair for intervals, such as [1, "day"]
---@alias sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseConfigSchedule string|sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseConfigScheduleCase1List

---@alias sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseConfigScheduleCase1List number[]

---Type of schedule: crontab or interval
---@alias sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseConfigScheduleType "crontab"|"interval"

---@class sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseEnvironmentsItem
---@field name string Name of the environment
---@field status sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseEnvironmentsItemStatus Status of the monitor in the environment
---@field isMuted boolean Whether incidents are muted for the monitor in the environment
---@field dateCreated string When the monitor was created (ISO 8601)
---@field lastCheckIn string|distilled.Null When the most recent check-in was received, not counting missed check-ins (ISO 8601)
---@field nextCheckIn string|distilled.Null When the next check-in is expected (ISO 8601)
---@field nextCheckInLatest string|distilled.Null Latest time the next check-in can arrive before it counts as missed (ISO 8601)
---@field activeIncident sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseEnvironmentsItemActiveIncident|distilled.Null Unresolved incident for the monitor in the environment. Null when there's none

---Unresolved incident for the monitor in the environment. Null when there's none
---@class sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseEnvironmentsItemActiveIncident
---@field startingTimestamp string|distilled.Null When the incident started (ISO 8601)
---@field resolvingTimestamp string|distilled.Null When the incident was resolved (ISO 8601)
---@field brokenNotice sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseEnvironmentsItemActiveIncidentBrokenNotice|distilled.Null Details of the broken monitor notice for the incident. Null when there's none

---Details of the broken monitor notice for the incident. Null when there's none
---@class sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseEnvironmentsItemActiveIncidentBrokenNotice
---@field userNotifiedTimestamp string|distilled.Null When users were notified that the monitor environment looks broken (ISO 8601)
---@field environmentMutedTimestamp string|distilled.Null When the broken monitor environment was muted (ISO 8601)

---Status of the monitor in the environment
---@alias sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseEnvironmentsItemStatus "active"|"disabled"|"pending_deletion"|"deletion_in_progress"|"ok"|"error"

---Environments the monitor has received check-ins for
---@alias sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseEnvironmentsList sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseEnvironmentsItem[]

---Team or user that owns the monitor. Null when there's no owner
---@class sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseOwner
---@field type sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseOwnerType Whether the actor is a user or a team
---@field id string ID of the user or team
---@field name string Display name of the user, or slug of the team
---@field email? string Email address of the user. Only set for users

---Whether the actor is a user or a team
---@alias sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseOwnerType "user"|"team"

---Project the monitor belongs to
---@class sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseProject
---@field stats? sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseProjectStats Counts of non-transaction events per interval over the requested stats period, as [timestamp, count] pairs. Only included when a stats period is requested
---@field transactionStats? sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseProjectTransactionStatsList Counts of transactions per interval over the requested stats period, as [timestamp, count] pairs. Only included when transaction stats are requested
---@field sessionStats? sentry.UpdateOrganizationMonitorResponseProjectSessionStats Crash-free session rates for the current and previous stats period. Only included when session stats are requested
---@field id string ID of the project
---@field slug string Slug of the project
---@field name string Name of the project
---@field platform string|distilled.Null Platform of the project
---@field dateCreated string When the project was created (ISO 8601)
---@field isBookmarked boolean Whether the requesting user bookmarked the project
