---@class sentry.UpdateOrganizationReleaseRequest
---@field organization_id_or_slug string The ID or slug of the organization the resource belongs to.
---@field version string The version identifier of the release
---@field ref? string|distilled.Null An optional commit reference. This is useful if a tagged version has been provided.
---@field url? string|distilled.Null A URL that points to the release. For instance, this can be the path to an online interface to the source code, such as a GitHub URL.
---@field dateReleased? string|distilled.Null An optional date that indicates when the release went live. If not provided the current time is used.
---@field commits? sentry.UpdateOrganizationReleaseRequestCommitsList An optional list of commit data to be associated. Very long lists are truncated to the most recent commits.
---@field status? string The status of the release. Can be `open` or `archived`.
---@field headCommits? sentry.UpdateOrganizationReleaseRequestHeadCommitsList Deprecated, use `commits`. Head commits to associate with the release.
---@field refs? sentry.UpdateOrganizationReleaseRequestRefsList An optional way to indicate the start and end commits for each repository included in a release. Head commits must include parameters ``repository`` and ``commit`` (the HEAD SHA). For GitLab repositories, please use the Group name instead of the slug. They can optionally include ``previousCommit`` (the SHA of the HEAD of the previous release), which should be specified if this is the first time you've sent commit data.

