---@field project string The project ID or slug to associate the monitor to.
---@field name string Name of the monitor. Used for notifications. If not set the slug will be derived from your monitor name.
---@field config sentry.UpdateProjectMonitorRequestConfig The configuration for the monitor.
---@field slug? string Uniquely identifies your monitor within your organization. Changing this slug will require updates to any instrumented check-in calls.
---@field status? sentry.UpdateProjectMonitorRequestStatus|string Status of the monitor. Disabled monitors will not accept events and will not count towards the monitor quota. * `active` * `disabled`
---@field owner? string|distilled.Null The ID of the team or user that owns the monitor. (eg. user:51 or team:6)
---@field is_muted? boolean Disable creation of monitor incidents

---@class sentry.UpdateProjectMonitorRequestConfig
---@field schedule_type? sentry.UpdateProjectMonitorRequestConfigScheduleType|string Currently supports "crontab" or "interval" * `crontab` * `interval`
---@field schedule any Varies depending on the schedule_type. Is either a crontab string, or a 2 element tuple for intervals (e.g. [1, 'day'])
---@field checkin_margin? number|distilled.Null How long (in minutes) after the expected checkin time will we wait until we consider the checkin to have been missed.
---@field max_runtime? number|distilled.Null How long (in minutes) is the checkin allowed to run for in CheckInStatus.IN_PROGRESS before it is considered failed. Maximum 10080 (7 days).
