---@class sentry.UpdateProjectRequest
---@field organization_id_or_slug string The ID or slug of the organization the resource belongs to.
---@field project_id_or_slug string The ID or slug of the project the resource belongs to. Project slugs are unique within each organization.
---@field digestsMinDelay number Minimum time in seconds to wait before sending an issue digest email.
---@field digestsMaxDelay number Maximum time in seconds to wait before sending an issue digest email.
---@field securityToken string Token sent with security reports (CSP, Expect-CT, HPKP) so Sentry can verify their origin.
---@field securityTokenHeader string Name of the header carrying the security token on inbound security reports.
---@field isBookmarked? boolean Enables starring the project within the projects tab. Can be updated with **`project:read`** permission.
---@field autofixAutomationTuning? sentry.UpdateProjectRequestAutofixAutomationTuning|string How aggressively Seer runs Autofix on new issues. Can be updated with **`project:read`** permission. * `off` * `super_low` * `low` * `medium` * `high` * `always`
---@field seerScannerAutomation? boolean Let Seer scan new issues automatically. Can be updated with **`project:read`** permission.
---@field preprodSizeStatusChecksEnabled? boolean Enable preprod size status checks. Can be updated with **`project:read`** permission.
---@field preprodSizeStatusChecksRules? sentry.UpdateProjectRequestPreprodSizeStatusChecksRulesMap Rules controlling when preprod size status checks fail. Can be updated with **`project:read`** permission.
---@field preprodSizePrCommentsEnabled? boolean Enable preprod size PR comments. Can be updated with **`project:read`** permission.
---@field preprodSizePrCommentsRules? sentry.UpdateProjectRequestPreprodSizePrCommentsRulesMap Rules controlling which preprod size changes are posted as PR comments. Can be updated with **`project:read`** permission.
---@field preprodSnapshotStatusChecksEnabled? boolean Enable preprod snapshot status checks.
---@field preprodSnapshotStatusChecksFailOnAdded? boolean Fail the preprod snapshot status check when snapshots are added.
---@field preprodSnapshotStatusChecksFailOnRemoved? boolean Fail the preprod snapshot status check when snapshots are removed.
---@field preprodSnapshotStatusChecksFailOnChanged? boolean Fail the preprod snapshot status check when snapshots change.
---@field preprodSnapshotStatusChecksFailOnRenamed? boolean Fail the preprod snapshot status check when snapshots are renamed.
---@field preprodSizeEnabledByCustomer? boolean|distilled.Null Enable preprod size analysis. Can be updated with **`project:read`** permission.
---@field preprodDistributionEnabledByCustomer? boolean|distilled.Null Enable preprod build distribution. Can be updated with **`project:read`** permission.
---@field preprodDistributionPrCommentsEnabledByCustomer? boolean|distilled.Null Post preprod distribution updates as PR comments. Can be updated with **`project:read`** permission.
---@field preprodSnapshotPrCommentsEnabled? boolean|distilled.Null Post preprod snapshot changes as PR comments.
---@field preprodSnapshotPrCommentsPostOnAdded? boolean|distilled.Null Include added snapshots in preprod snapshot PR comments.
---@field preprodSnapshotPrCommentsPostOnRemoved? boolean|distilled.Null Include removed snapshots in preprod snapshot PR comments.
---@field preprodSnapshotPrCommentsPostOnChanged? boolean|distilled.Null Include changed snapshots in preprod snapshot PR comments.
---@field preprodSnapshotPrCommentsPostOnRenamed? boolean|distilled.Null Include renamed snapshots in preprod snapshot PR comments.
---@field preprodSizeEnabledQuery? string|distilled.Null Query selecting which preprod builds are size-analyzed. Can be updated with **`project:read`** permission.
---@field preprodDistributionEnabledQuery? string|distilled.Null Query selecting which preprod builds are distributed. Can be updated with **`project:read`** permission.
---@field name? string The name for the project
---@field slug? string Uniquely identifies a project and is used for the interface.
---@field platform? string|distilled.Null The platform for the project
---@field subjectPrefix? string Custom prefix for emails from this project.
---@field subjectTemplate? string The email subject to use (excluding the prefix) for individual alerts. Here are the list of variables you can use: - `$title` - `$shortID` - `$projectID` - `$orgID` - `${tag:key}` - such as `${tag:environment}` or `${tag:release}`.
---@field resolveAge? number|distilled.Null Automatically resolve an issue if it hasn't been seen for this many hours. Set to `0` to disable auto-resolve.
---@field highlightContext? sentry.UpdateProjectRequestHighlightContextMap A JSON mapping of context types to lists of strings for their keys. E.g. `{'user': ['id', 'email']}`
---@field highlightTags? sentry.UpdateProjectRequestHighlightTagsList A list of strings with tag keys to highlight on this project's issues. E.g. `['release', 'environment']`
---@field verifySSL? boolean Verify SSL certificates when delivering outbound webhooks and service hooks.
---@field defaultEnvironment? string|distilled.Null Environment selected by default when viewing this project.
---@field dataScrubber? boolean Remove known sensitive values from events before storing them.
---@field dataScrubberDefaults? boolean Also scrub Sentry's built-in list of sensitive field names.
---@field sensitiveFields? sentry.UpdateProjectRequestSensitiveFieldsList Additional field names to scrub from events, beyond the defaults.
---@field safeFields? sentry.UpdateProjectRequestSafeFieldsList Field names to exempt from scrubbing, including the built-in defaults.
